<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jabala ibn al-Ayham</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jabala ibn al-Ayham was the last king of the Ghassanids, the Christian Arab allies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> on the Syrian frontier. He led Ghassanid forces for Byzantium against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, including at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-yarmuk">Battle of the Yarmuk</a> in 636. According to Arab tradition he briefly converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> but then renounced it and withdrew with his followers into Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, where he died.</p></div>
